---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
---
<ToolLayout
  slug="dns-propagation"
  title="DNS Propagation Check"
  description="Compare a DNS record across two independent resolvers — Cloudflare and Google — to see whether your change has taken effect or a stale cache is still serving the old answer."
  heading="DNS propagation check"
  intro="Query the same record at two independent public resolvers and compare the answers. If they agree, your change is live where it matters most; if they differ, one of them is usually still serving a cached copy — and the remaining TTL tells you how long that lasts."
>
  <div slot="input" class="dp-bar">
    <div class="dp-fields">
      <div class="dp-field dp-field-name">
        <label for="dp-name">Name to query</label>
        <input
          id="dp-name"
          type="text"
          inputmode="url"
          autocomplete="off"
          spellcheck="false"
          placeholder="www.example.com"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="dp-field dp-field-type">
        <label for="dp-type">Record type</label>
        <select id="dp-type">
          <option value="A" selected>A</option>
          <option value="AAAA">AAAA</option>
          <option value="CNAME">CNAME</option>
          <option value="MX">MX</option>
          <option value="TXT">TXT</option>
          <option value="NS">NS</option>
          <option value="SOA">SOA</option>
          <option value="CAA">CAA</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <button id="dp-run" type="button" class="btn btn-primary">
        <Icon name="pulse" size={16} />
        <span id="dp-run-label">Compare resolvers</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <p class="dp-scope">
      <Icon name="shield" size={14} />
      <span>
        <strong>Two resolvers, not twenty.</strong> Only Cloudflare (1.1.1.1) and Google (8.8.8.8)
        publish DoH endpoints a browser is allowed to read. Quad9 and AdGuard block cross-origin
        requests, so no honest browser-only tool can include them — and none of this runs from
        other countries. Everything here happens in your tab.
      </span>
    </p>

    <p id="dp-msg" class="dp-msg mono" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </div>

  <section class="section dp-sec">
    <div class="container">
      <div id="dp-verdict" class="dp-verdict">
        <p class="dp-idle">Enter a name and record type above to compare answers.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="dp-cards" class="dp-cards"></div>

      <div class="glass-card dp-limits">
        <div class="dp-limits-head">
          <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="shield" size={18} /></span>
          <h2 class="h3">What this check can and cannot tell you</h2>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>It compares two caches, not the world.</strong> Server-backed checkers query
            20+ resolvers from 20+ countries. This page is limited to the two endpoints that permit
            browser requests. Two independent resolvers still catch the failure that matters most —
            one of them holding a stale answer.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Both resolvers are anycast.</strong> Your query lands on the node nearest to
            you, so a match proves those two networks agree <em>as seen from your location</em>. A
            resolver in another region may still hold a different cached copy.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Some records differ on purpose, permanently.</strong> Google's resolver forwards
            your approximate network location to the authoritative server (EDNS Client Subnet);
            Cloudflare's deliberately does not. Anything behind a CDN, or using latency-based or
            geographic routing, therefore hands the two resolvers different answers by design — and
            no amount of waiting makes them converge. A mismatch that outlives the longer TTL shown
            below is routing, not propagation.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Neither answer is authoritative.</strong> DoH gives you a recursive resolver's
            cached view, and neither endpoint exposes a cache-bypass flag. To confirm what your
            nameservers actually publish you need <code class="mono">dig @ns1.yourprovider.net</code>
            — a browser cannot open a raw DNS socket to an arbitrary server.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Response times are not a latency benchmark.</strong> The millisecond figure
            includes TLS setup and HTTP overhead, and a cache miss costs far more than a hit. Read
            it as a rough health signal, not a measurement.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your own machine is a third cache.</strong> Your OS, your browser and your
            router may all still hold the old record even when both resolvers here agree.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dp-notes-sec">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Field notes</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Nothing propagates. Caches expire.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          The word "propagation" invents a process that does not exist, and it is the reason people
          wait passively for something that was already finished hours ago.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-3 dp-notes">
        <article class="glass-card">
          <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="route" size={20} /></span>
          <h3 class="h3">There is no wave to wait for</h3>
          <p>
            When you edit a zone, the change is live at your authoritative nameservers the moment
            they reload — usually seconds. Nothing is pushed anywhere. What you are actually waiting
            on is every recursive resolver that already asked, each holding your old answer until
            the TTL it was handed runs out. Those countdowns started at different moments, which is
            precisely why two resolvers can disagree for a while and both be behaving correctly.
          </p>
          <p>
            So a mismatch here is not a fault to chase. The only question worth asking is
            <em>which TTL is still running</em>, and the answer is on the card that shows the old
            value.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="glass-card">
          <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="clock" size={20} /></span>
          <h3 class="h3">Lower the TTL a day before you move</h3>
          <p>
            The professional technique is planned, not reactive. Roughly 24–48 hours before a
            migration, drop the TTL on the records you intend to change to
            <code class="mono">300</code>. Wait out the <em>old</em> TTL — if it was 86400, resolvers
            need a full day to pick up the new short one. Only then cut over: your worst-case
            exposure is now five minutes instead of a day.
          </p>
          <p>
            Once the change is verified and stable, raise it back to 3600 or higher. Permanently low
            TTLs mean more lookups, more latency on cold hits, and a hard dependency on your DNS
            provider staying reachable. Low TTL is a manoeuvre, not a default.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="glass-card">
          <span class="icon-tile"><Icon name="shield" size={20} /></span>
          <h3 class="h3">Negative caching is the one that surprises you</h3>
          <p>
            Query a record before it exists and the resolver caches the <em>absence</em>. How long
            depends on the zone's SOA — the minimum field, capped by the SOA record's own TTL — and
            SOA minimums of 3600 are common while the record's TTL might be 300. Create the record,
            re-check, and it can stay missing for an hour even though publication was instant.
          </p>
          <p>
            This is why "it works for my colleague but not for me" happens right after a launch: one
            of you tested early and poisoned your resolver's negative cache. The fix is patience or a
            different resolver — and the prevention is not querying a name until you have created it.
            Where this page returns NXDOMAIN it shows the negative TTL so you know the real wait.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="glass-card dp-reading">
        <h3 class="h3">Reading a disagreement</h3>
        <p>
          Answer order carries no meaning in DNS. A resolver that returns three A records will
          rotate them between queries on purpose, to spread load — this tool sorts both answer sets
          before comparing them, so rotation is never reported as a mismatch. Only the
          <em>contents</em> of the sets are compared, and long TXT strings split across quoted
          segments are joined first, because consumers concatenate them anyway.
        </p>
        <p>
          Two kinds of disagreement are <em>not</em> cache problems, and both are permanent. NS and
          SOA records that differ between resolvers usually mean the zone is hosted at two DNS
          providers at once, so each resolver reports whichever authoritative side answered it.
          Differing SOA serial numbers between providers are normal. Check whether the nameserver
          hostnames belong to two vendors before you start waiting for something to settle.
        </p>
        <p>
          The other is the common one, and it catches people out: A and AAAA records that differ
          because the <em>resolver</em> differs. Google's 8.8.8.8 passes your approximate network
          location to the authoritative server as EDNS Client Subnet; Cloudflare's 1.1.1.1 refuses
          to, on privacy grounds. Any CDN or latency-routed record will answer those two queries
          differently and keep doing so forever, so a stable mismatch on a CDN-fronted name means
          your traffic is being steered, not that a cache is stale. The test is simple: note the
          longer TTL, wait it out, re-check. A cache converges; routing does not.
        </p>
        <p>
          The genuinely interesting outcome is one resolver answering NXDOMAIN while the other
          resolves. That is mid-propagation in its clearest form: one cache learned "no such name"
          before you published, the other learned the record afterwards. If instead <em>both</em>
          resolvers return SERVFAIL, stop thinking about caches — that points at a broken delegation
          or a DNSSEC validation failure, and no amount of waiting will fix it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ToolLayout>

<style>
  .dp-bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }

  .dp-fields {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .dp-field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .dp-field-name { flex: 1 1 20rem; min-width: 0; }
  .dp-field-type { flex: 0 0 9.5rem; }

  .dp-field label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .dp-field input,
  .dp-field select {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    transition: border-color 0.18s var(--ease-out);
  }

  .dp-field input:focus,
  .dp-field select:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--accent-blue);
  }

  #dp-run { flex: 0 0 auto; }
  #dp-run[disabled] { cursor: progress; opacity: 0.7; }

  .dp-scope {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-violet);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--text-soft);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .dp-scope :global(svg) { flex: 0 0 auto; margin-top: 0.25rem; color: var(--accent-violet); }
  .dp-scope strong { color: var(--text); }

  .dp-msg {
    min-height: 1.2em;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .dp-msg[data-tone='bad'] { color: var(--accent-red); }

  /* Verdict and cards are injected by script, so descendants need :global(). */
  .dp-verdict { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }

  .dp-idle {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .dp-verdict :global(.dp-v) {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-blue);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--bg-elev);
  }

  .dp-verdict :global(.dp-v-good) { border-left-color: var(--accent-cyan); }
  .dp-verdict :global(.dp-v-warn) { border-left-color: var(--accent-violet); }
  .dp-verdict :global(.dp-v-bad) { border-left-color: var(--accent-red); }

  .dp-verdict :global(.dp-v-title) {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .dp-verdict :global(.dp-v-detail) {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 68ch;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .dp-verdict :global(.dp-v-diff) {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }

  .dp-verdict :global(.dp-v-diff > div) {
    flex: 1 1 16rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .dp-verdict :global(.dp-v-diff h4) {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .dp-verdict :global(.dp-v-diff code) {
    display: block;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text);
    white-space: pre;
  }

  .dp-cards {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 22rem), 1fr));
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-card) {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--surface-strong);
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-card-head) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-card-head h3) {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-addr) {
    padding: 0.1rem 0.45rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-ms) {
    margin-left: auto;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-dot) {
    width: 0.6rem;
    height: 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-dot-good) { background: var(--accent-cyan); }
  .dp-cards :global(.dp-dot-warn) { background: var(--accent-violet); }
  .dp-cards :global(.dp-dot-bad) { background: var(--accent-red); }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-status) {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  /* Fixed dark terminal palette: record values stay legible in light theme too. */
  .dp-cards :global(.dp-recs) {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--term-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--term-bg);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-rec) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-rtype) {
    flex: 0 0 3.75rem;
    color: var(--term-cmd);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-rdata) { color: var(--term-ok); }
  .dp-cards :global(.dp-rec-chain .dp-rdata) { color: var(--term-text); }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-rttl) {
    margin-left: auto;
    padding-left: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--term-accent);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-empty) {
    color: var(--term-text);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-ttl-note) {
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-soft);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .dp-cards :global(.dp-ttl-note strong) { color: var(--text); }

  .dp-limits {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .dp-limits-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }

  .dp-limits-head h2 { margin: 0; }

  .dp-limits ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .dp-limits strong { color: var(--text); }
  .dp-limits code,
  .dp-notes code,
  .dp-reading code {
    padding: 0.05rem 0.35rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    background: var(--surface);
    font-size: 0.88em;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .dp-notes article p {
    color: var(--text-soft);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .dp-notes article p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .dp-reading {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .dp-reading p {
    max-width: 78ch;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .dp-reading p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .dp-fields { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
    .dp-field-type { flex: 1 1 auto; }
    #dp-run { width: 100%; justify-content: center; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { esc } from '../../scripts/tool-ui.js';
  import { isValidDomain } from '../../scripts/email-scan.js';
  import {
    RESOLVERS,
    checkPropagation,
    compareResults,
    fmtSeconds,
    isQueryableName,
    normaliseName,
    rcodeName,
    typeCode,
    typeName,
  } from '../../scripts/dns-propagate.js';

  const nameEl = document.getElementById('dp-name');
  const typeEl = document.getElementById('dp-type');
  const runEl = document.getElementById('dp-run');
  const runLabelEl = document.getElementById('dp-run-label');
  const msgEl = document.getElementById('dp-msg');
  const verdictEl = document.getElementById('dp-verdict');
  const cardsEl = document.getElementById('dp-cards');

  if (nameEl && typeEl && runEl && msgEl && verdictEl && cardsEl) {
    const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
    const preName = normaliseName(params.get('name') || params.get('domain') || '');
    if (preName) nameEl.value = preName;
    const preType = String(params.get('type') || '').toUpperCase();
    if (typeCode(preType)) typeEl.value = preType;

    let busy = false;

    function setMsg(text, tone) {
      msgEl.textContent = text;
      if (tone) msgEl.dataset.tone = tone;
      else delete msgEl.dataset.tone;
    }

    function toneFor(state) {
      if (state === 'error' || state === 'rcode') return 'bad';
      if (state === 'nxdomain' || state === 'nodata') return 'warn';
      return 'good';
    }

    function statusLine(r, code) {
      if (r.state === 'error') return esc(r.error || 'Request failed');
      const n = r.matching.length;
      const extra = r.records.length - n;
      if (r.state === 'nxdomain') return 'NXDOMAIN — no such name';
      if (r.state === 'nodata') return 'NOERROR — no records of this type';
      if (r.state === 'rcode') return `${esc(rcodeName(r.status))} — resolver could not answer`;
      const chain = extra > 0 ? ` (+${extra} in chain)` : '';
      return `NOERROR — ${n} ${esc(typeName(code))} record${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}${chain}`;
    }

    function recsHtml(r, code) {
      if (r.state === 'error') {
        return `<div class="dp-recs"><span class="dp-empty">no data</span></div>`;
      }
      if (r.state === 'rcode') {
        // Not an empty answer: the resolver failed, so there is nothing to cache.
        return `<div class="dp-recs"><span class="dp-empty">no answer — ${esc(rcodeName(r.status))}</span></div>`;
      }
      if (!r.records.length) {
        const neg = Number.isFinite(r.negTtl) ? r.negTtl : NaN;
        const negTxt = Number.isFinite(neg)
          ? `empty answer — negative cache ${fmtSeconds(neg)}`
          : 'empty answer';
        return `<div class="dp-recs"><span class="dp-empty">${esc(negTxt)}</span></div>`;
      }
      const rows = r.records.map((rec) => {
        const chain = rec.type !== code ? ' dp-rec-chain' : '';
        const ttl = Number.isFinite(rec.ttl) ? `${rec.ttl}s` : '—';
        return `<div class="dp-rec${chain}">`
          + `<span class="dp-rtype">${esc(typeName(rec.type))}</span>`
          + `<span class="dp-rdata">${esc(rec.data)}</span>`
          + `<span class="dp-rttl">TTL ${esc(ttl)}</span>`
          + `</div>`;
      }).join('');
      return `<div class="dp-recs">${rows}</div>`;
    }

    function ttlNote(r) {
      if (r.state === 'error') {
        return 'No answer, so no cache state to report.';
      }
      if (r.state === 'nxdomain' || r.state === 'nodata') {
        const parts = [];
        if (Number.isFinite(r.negTtl)) {
          parts.push(`this negative answer is cached for up to <strong>${esc(fmtSeconds(r.negTtl))}</strong>`);
        }
        if (Number.isFinite(r.soaMinimum)) {
          parts.push(`zone SOA minimum is ${esc(fmtSeconds(r.soaMinimum))}`);
        }
        return parts.length
          ? `Negative caching: ${parts.join(', ')}. A record created now can stay invisible here until then.`
          : 'Negative caching applies: the absence of this record is itself cached.';
      }
      if (!Number.isFinite(r.ttl)) return 'No TTL reported for this answer.';
      return `Remaining TTL <strong>${esc(fmtSeconds(r.ttl))}</strong> — this resolver will keep serving the answer above for up to that long before it asks again. That is your worst-case wait here.`;
    }

    function cardHtml(r, code) {
      return `<article class="dp-card">`
        + `<div class="dp-card-head">`
        + `<span class="dp-dot dp-dot-${toneFor(r.state)}"></span>`
        + `<h3>${esc(r.label)}</h3>`
        + `<span class="dp-addr mono">${esc(r.addr)}</span>`
        + `<span class="dp-ms mono">${esc(String(r.ms))} ms</span>`
        + `</div>`
        + `<p class="dp-status">${statusLine(r, code)}</p>`
        + recsHtml(r, code)
        + `<p class="dp-ttl-note">${ttlNote(r)}</p>`
        + `</article>`;
    }

    function verdictHtml(v) {
      let diff = '';
      const blocks = [];
      if (Array.isArray(v.diff)) {
        v.diff.forEach((d) => {
          if (d.items.length) {
            blocks.push(`<div><h4>Only from ${esc(d.label)}</h4><code>${d.items.map(esc).join('\n')}</code></div>`);
          }
        });
      } else if (Array.isArray(v.only) && v.only.length) {
        blocks.push(`<div><h4>Only from ${esc(v.onlyLabel)}</h4><code>${v.only.map(esc).join('\n')}</code></div>`);
      }
      if (blocks.length) diff = `<div class="dp-v-diff">${blocks.join('')}</div>`;
      return `<div class="dp-v dp-v-${esc(v.tone)}">`
        + `<p class="dp-v-title">${esc(v.title)}</p>`
        + `<p class="dp-v-detail">${esc(v.detail)}</p>`
        + diff
        + `</div>`;
    }

    function pending(name, typeLabel) {
      verdictEl.innerHTML = `<div class="dp-v"><p class="dp-v-title">Querying ${esc(name)} ${esc(typeLabel)}…</p>`
        + `<p class="dp-v-detail">Both resolvers are being asked in parallel.</p></div>`;
      cardsEl.innerHTML = RESOLVERS.map((r) => `<article class="dp-card">`
        + `<div class="dp-card-head"><span class="dp-dot"></span><h3>${esc(r.label)}</h3>`
        + `<span class="dp-addr mono">${esc(r.addr)}</span></div>`
        + `<p class="dp-status">waiting for answer…</p></article>`).join('');
    }

    async function run() {
      if (busy) return;
      const raw = nameEl.value;
      const name = normaliseName(raw);
      if (!name) {
        setMsg('Enter a domain or hostname first.', 'bad');
        nameEl.focus();
        return;
      }
      if (!isQueryableName(name) && !isValidDomain(name)) {
        setMsg(`"${name}" is not a queryable DNS name — expected something like www.example.com.`, 'bad');
        return;
      }
      const typeLabel = typeEl.value;
      const code = typeCode(typeLabel);
      if (!code) {
        setMsg('Pick a supported record type.', 'bad');
        return;
      }

      busy = true;
      runEl.disabled = true;
      // Only the label span may be rewritten — runEl also holds the icon SVG.
      const label = runLabelEl ? runLabelEl.textContent : '';
      if (runLabelEl) runLabelEl.textContent = 'Checking…';
      setMsg(`Querying ${name} ${typeLabel} at ${RESOLVERS.length} resolvers…`);
      pending(name, typeLabel);

      try {
        const results = await checkPropagation(name, code);
        cardsEl.innerHTML = results.map((r) => cardHtml(r, code)).join('');
        verdictEl.innerHTML = verdictHtml(compareResults(results[0], results[1], code));
        const slowest = Math.max(...results.map((r) => r.ms || 0));
        setMsg(`${name} ${typeLabel} — checked at ${new Date().toLocaleTimeString()} (slowest resolver ${slowest} ms)`);
      } catch (err) {
        // checkPropagation is designed not to reject; this is the last-resort net.
        cardsEl.innerHTML = '';
        verdictEl.innerHTML = `<div class="dp-v dp-v-bad"><p class="dp-v-title">The check could not complete</p>`
          + `<p class="dp-v-detail">${esc(err && err.message ? err.message : 'Unexpected error.')} Re-run it, or try another network — DoH is sometimes blocked by filtering proxies and privacy extensions.</p></div>`;
        setMsg('Check failed. Nothing was compared.', 'bad');
      } finally {
        busy = false;
        runEl.disabled = false;
        if (runLabelEl) runLabelEl.textContent = label;
      }
    }

    runEl.addEventListener('click', run);
    nameEl.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (e.key === 'Enter') {
        e.preventDefault();
        run();
      }
    });
    typeEl.addEventListener('change', () => {
      if (nameEl.value.trim()) run();
    });
  }
</script>
